Z||000002||theogre||11-09-2001||06:14 PM||||try the form info at <A HREF="http://www.WebMonkey.com" TARGET=_blank>www.WebMonkey.com</A>  or cnet's <A HREF="http://www.builder.com" TARGET=_blank>www.builder.com</A>  Both have clear explanations of how to prefill the TO CC BCC and Subject lines of mailto links and forms.<P>Note that in most cases... true forms require CGI or something to run on the server. Exactly what gets filled in how depends on what CGI etc, is on the server. There can be quite a bit of variation.<P>mailto is all client side and simply opens the user's email program with the above mentioned lines already filled in for the user. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
